---
// Look-ahead in an LLM backtest (Glasserman and Lin 2023). Say a model was trained on text up to the end of 2022
// and you backtest news sentiment on 2021-2023 headlines. Headlines from 2021-2022 sit inside its training text:
// it may already "know" how those stories ended. Only 2023 is clean. Dates are chosen for the example.
import DiagramIcon from './DiagramIcon.astro';
const X0 = 60;
const X1 = 860;
const years = [2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024];
const xOf = (y: number) => X0 + ((y - 2020) / 4) * (X1 - X0);
---
<figure class="a21a">
  <div class="a21a-scroll">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 900 330" role="img" aria-label="A timeline from 2020 to 2024. Say a language model was trained on text up to the end of 2022. A backtest on headlines from 2021 to 2023 has two years inside the model's training text, where it may already know how the stories ended, and one clean year, 2023, after its cutoff. Two remedies: hide company names, and test only after the cutoff.">
      <text x="20" y="28" class="a21a-h"><tspan data-lang-en>The model may have read the ending before your backtest starts</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Model có thể đã đọc phần kết trước khi backtest của bạn bắt đầu</tspan></text>
      <rect x={xOf(2020)} y="56" width={xOf(2023) - xOf(2020)} height="44" class="a21a-train" />
      <DiagramIcon name="model" x={xOf(2020) + 24} y="78" size={22} />
      <text x={xOf(2020) + 46} y="83" class="a21a-t"><tspan data-lang-en>Model's training text, ends Dec 2022</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Văn bản huấn luyện của model, đến hết 12/2022</tspan></text>
      <rect x={xOf(2021)} y="116" width={xOf(2023) - xOf(2021)} height="44" class="a21a-bt is-leak" />
      <rect x={xOf(2023)} y="116" width={xOf(2024) - xOf(2023)} height="44" class="a21a-bt is-clean" />
      <text x={xOf(2021) + 12} y="143" class="a21a-t"><tspan data-lang-en>Backtest 2021-2022: leak risk</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Backtest 2021-2022: nguy cơ rò rỉ</tspan></text>
      <text x={xOf(2023) + 12} y="143" class="a21a-t"><tspan data-lang-en>2023: clean</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>2023: sạch</tspan></text>
      <line x1={xOf(2023)} y1="48" x2={xOf(2023)} y2="176" class="a21a-cut" />
      <text x={xOf(2023) + 6} y="190" class="a21a-cutt"><tspan data-lang-en>training cutoff</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>mốc cắt huấn luyện</tspan></text>
      <line x1={X0} y1="206" x2={X1} y2="206" class="a21a-axis" />
      {years.map((y) => (
        <g>
          <line x1={xOf(y)} y1="200" x2={xOf(y)} y2="212" class="a21a-axis" />
          <text x={xOf(y)} y="228" text-anchor="middle" class="a21a-s">{y}</text>
        </g>
      ))}
      <rect x="20" y="248" width="420" height="64" rx="8" class="a21a-fix" />
      <text x="34" y="272" class="a21a-t"><tspan data-lang-en>Remedy 1: hide the company name</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Cách 1: giấu tên công ty</tspan></text>
      <text x="34" y="292" class="a21a-s"><tspan data-lang-en>Glasserman and Lin: anonymised headlines scored better.</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Glasserman và Lin: tiêu đề ẩn danh cho kết quả tốt hơn.</tspan></text>
      <rect x="460" y="248" width="420" height="64" rx="8" class="a21a-fix" />
      <text x="474" y="272" class="a21a-t"><tspan data-lang-en>Remedy 2: score only after the cutoff</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Cách 2: chỉ chấm sau mốc cắt</tspan></text>
      <text x="474" y="292" class="a21a-s"><tspan data-lang-en>Then the model cannot have seen the outcome.</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>Khi đó model không thể đã thấy kết quả.</tspan></text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>Say a model's text ends in December 2022 and you test it on 2021 to 2023 headlines. Two of those three years are inside what it read. The dates are an example; check the cutoff of the model you use.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Giả sử văn bản của model dừng ở tháng 12/2022 và bạn thử nó trên tiêu đề 2021 đến 2023. Hai trong ba năm nằm trong những gì nó đã đọc. Các mốc là ví dụ; hãy tra mốc cắt của model bạn dùng.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .a21a { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .a21a-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .a21a svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 700px; height: auto; }
  .a21a text { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text-body); }
  .a21a .a21a-h { font-size: 16px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .a21a .a21a-t { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .a21a .a21a-s { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .a21a .a21a-cutt { font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; fill: var(--red); }
  .a21a-train { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .a21a-bt { stroke: var(--bg); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .a21a-bt.is-leak { fill: var(--red-tint-bg); stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .a21a-bt.is-clean { fill: var(--gold-tint-bg); stroke: var(--gold-icon); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .a21a-cut { stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.6; stroke-dasharray: 5 4; }
  .a21a-axis { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .a21a-fix { fill: var(--bg-alt); stroke: var(--gold-icon); stroke-width: 1.3; }
  .a21a figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
